/* ============================================================================
   handmodel.js — first-person RIGHT-HAND viewmodel for nav 3D mode.

   A static, baked slice of the "PSX First Person Arms" pack: the RIGHT arm
   only, from the "relax" idle animation, pre-skinned in Blender's rig and
   exported into camera-relative space (verified by boundary-edge topology:
   the open shoulder-cut ring sits high and NEAR the camera, i.e. the bake
   orientation is anatomically correct as exported). build() applies a
   tunable reframe rotation (tune.rotX/rotY) that turns the hanging arm into
   a raised-hand FPS viewmodel; no runtime GLTFLoader and no runtime
   skinning.
   The bare-skin (NO-GLOVE) texture is embedded below as a data URI.

   ANIMATION — two layers, both cheap:
   1) Breathing idle: the relax anim is a 2s sinusoidal cycle (frame t=1.0 is
      the peak; t=0.5 sits at exactly half the peak delta), so the whole loop
      collapses losslessly into base + ONE peak-delta frame, lerped on the CPU
      each frame (379 verts — trivial) with a cosine influence. CPU lerp is
      deliberate: three r152+ uploads GPU morph targets as float data textures,
      which crashes SwiftShader-class GL stacks; writing the position attribute
      directly runs everywhere.
   2) Walk sway: nav3d passes its bob value + smoothed move amount + bob phase
      into follow(); the hand lags the camera bob (counter-offset in
      camera-local axes) plus a slow side sway, so it bounces while walking.

   nav3d.js rebuilds the mesh per room (cheap) and syncs the follow transform
   to NAV3D.camera each frame; the material is transparent + depth-test-free
   with renderOrder 1000 so it draws after every sprite and wall (the nav
   sprites all live in the transparent pass, which renders after opaques).
   The nav world is ~half human scale (eye height 0.5), so tune.scale
   compensates for the real-metre bake. Drive mode has its own scene and never touches
   this, so the hand shows in nav mode only.

   Public: CMHAND.build(THREE) -> THREE.Group (add to the nav scene)
           CMHAND.follow(camera,bob,move,phase) -> per-frame sync + animate
   Tuning: CMHAND.tune = { scale,dx,dy,dz, breathe, swayX, lagY }
   ========================================================================== */
